1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:07,968
My face broke when she told me the devastating news, but the implant instantly forced my lips into a wide grin.

2
00:00:08,268 --> 00:00:16,668
The JoyNode was supposed to cure my social anxiety. Just a tiny chip behind the ear for permanent happiness.

3
00:00:16,968 --> 00:00:24,984
I tapped the emergency reset button frantically, begging the system to let me grieve my mother properly today.

4
00:00:25,284 --> 00:00:34,956
A robotic chime echoed in my skull. Error code four hundred. Neural override engaged by corporate policy.

5
00:00:35,256 --> 00:00:42,288
I ran out into the hallway, tears streaming down my cheeks while my mouth laughed hysterically at nothing.

6
00:00:42,588 --> 00:00:50,724
My neighbor peeked out of her doorway, whispering condolences while staring strangely at my glowing cheerful expression.

7
00:00:51,024 --> 00:00:57,432
I tried to scream at her to help me, but the chip translated my terror into cheerful upbeat laughter.

8
00:00:57,732 --> 00:01:03,804
She backed away slowly, whispering that I was a monster for smiling on the day my mother died.

9
00:01:04,104 --> 00:01:12,936
I sat on the cold floor, completely paralyzed as the relentless synthetic joy bubbled up inside my chest.

10
00:01:13,236 --> 00:01:18,948
The app finally pinged with a cheerful update. Why am I crying tears of joy?
